# Byte-for-byte reproducibility.
#
# The frozen prompt pool carries a sha256 in data/MANIFEST.json, and the cloud
# box re-verifies it at startup (src/data.py:load_pool). A checkout that
# rewrites line endings makes that hash differ and aborts the run, so text is
# normalised to LF in the repo AND checked out as LF on every OS.
#
# See DEVLOG.md D-09: the first commit stored the pool as LF while the manifest
# recorded the CRLF hash, which would have failed on any Linux clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# never touch these
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.pt   binary
*.bin  binary
*.safetensors binary
*.npz  binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary
